#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:1
msgid "Fitparameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:3
msgid ""
"PySME can use a wide variety of fitparameters, however there are a few "
"things to consider."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:6
msgid "How to specify fitparameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:8
msgid ""
"Fitparameters can either be passed to `pysme.solve.solve` or as part of "
"the sme structure. When in doubt the explicitly passed values overwrite "
"the structure. Fitparameters are passed using their names as strings "
"(e.g. `'teff'` or `'logg'`), which are usually straightforward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:13
msgid ""
"There are however a few more tricky ones for individual abundances and "
"linelist parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:16
msgid "Abundances"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:17
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Individual abundances are passed using strings of the form `'abund {El}'`"
" where `'El'` is the short form element we want to fit (e.g. `'Mg'`). "
"PySME supports the fitting of all elements up to `'Es'`. Alternatively "
"you can also use the element number, i.e. the charge number, instead; "
"e.g. `'3'` for Lithium."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:24
msgid "Linelist"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:25
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For linelist parameters use `'linelist {nr} {p}'`, where `'nr'` is the "
"index in the linelist and `'p'` is the name of the parameter (e.g. "
"`'gflog'`). Parameters of the long format (e.g. lande_upper) can only be "
"varied for a long format linelist. For a list of the linelist parameters,"
" see [](linelist)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:32
msgid "Bounds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:34
msgid ""
"Most parameters have bounds. PySME gets the bounds of each parameter from"
" the specified atmosphere grid if possible. It also only allows for "
"positive turbulence velocities for example."
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:38
msgid "Continuum and Radial velocities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../concepts/fitparameters.md:41
msgid ""
"It might be logical to think that the continuum and especially the radial"
" velocity is a regular fitparameters. However there are several options "
"about how to handle them (see [here](./sme_struct.md#radial-velocity-and-"
"continuum)). It is therefore recommended to use `'cscale_flag'` and "
"`'vrad_flag'` to specify the desired fitting method. If `'vrad'` is "
"passed as a fitparameter it is equivalent to `'vrad_flag' = 'each'`, and "
"if `'cont'` is passed it is the same as `'cscale_flag' = 'linear'`. See "
"the [radial velocity](../fundamentals/rv.md) and "
"[continuum](../fundamentals/continuum.md) page for more information."
msgstr ""

